Empty pairs are text: {//} {**} {__} {~~} {^^} {,,} {==} {++} {##}.\n -> source.carve
\n -> source.carve
A pair that holds something is the construct:  -> source.carve
{/ -> source.carve markup.italic.carve keyword.control.italic.carve
i -> source.carve markup.italic.carve markup.italic.carve
/} -> source.carve markup.italic.carve keyword.control.italic.carve
  -> source.carve
{* -> source.carve markup.bold.carve keyword.control.bold.carve
b -> source.carve markup.bold.carve markup.bold.carve
*} -> source.carve markup.bold.carve keyword.control.bold.carve
  -> source.carve
{~ -> source.carve markup.deleted.carve keyword.control.strike.carve
s -> source.carve markup.deleted.carve markup.deleted.carve
~} -> source.carve markup.deleted.carve keyword.control.strike.carve
  -> source.carve
{+ -> source.carve markup.inserted.critic.carve keyword.control.critic.carve
ins -> source.carve markup.inserted.critic.carve markup.inserted.carve
+} -> source.carve markup.inserted.critic.carve keyword.control.critic.carve
  -> source.carve
{# -> source.carve comment.block.critic.carve keyword.control.critic.carve
